INT. DRAINED SWIMMING POOL - COMMUNITY CENTER - DAWN

Cracked blue tile. A dry deep end littered with leaves. Floodlights on stands. Yellow tape across the diving board.

DETECTIVE CASSIUS RHEE, 40s, rain jacket, notebook, crouches at the bottom of the deep end beside a chalk outline. FORENSIC TECH BELINDA OSEI, 30s, white suit, kneels with a camera. A tarp covers something near the drain.

RHEE
Time of death?

OSEI
Medical examiner says midnight. Give or take.

RHEE
Who drained the pool?

OSEI
Nobody. It's been empty since August.

RHEE
Then how did she end up down here?

OSEI
She fell. Or she was pushed.

He steps over the chalk. Lifts the tarp with a pen. Underneath, a single red high-heeled shoe.

RHEE
Where's the other?

OSEI
Haven't found it.

A phone rings. Rhee's. He answers.

CAPTAIN VOSS (V.O.)
(tinny, over the phone)
Rhee. Anything?

RHEE
A shoe, Captain. Just a shoe.

CAPTAIN VOSS (V.O.)
There's a witness on her way down. Janitor. Says she saw something.

RHEE
Copy.

He hangs up. Footsteps on the stairs. A figure descends: MS. DOLORES AMADI, 60s, janitor's apron, mop in hand like a staff. She stops at the pool edge.

DOLORES
Detective?

RHEE
Ms. Amadi. Come down.

She picks her way down the shallow-end steps, mop first.

DOLORES
I saw a man. By the diving board. Very tall. Very quiet.

OSEI
What was he wearing?

DOLORES
Gray. A long coat. Like a priest.

RHEE
Did he see you?

DOLORES
No. But he left something.

She reaches into her apron pocket. Pulls out the second red shoe, wrapped in a plastic bag. Rhee and Osei exchange a look.

OSEI
You touched it?

DOLORES
I wore gloves.

RHEE
(taking it)
Thank you.

A clang from the diving board. All three whip around. The tape trembles. A silhouette stands at the top of the board, backlit by dawn.

RHEE (CONT'D)
(low)
Police! Stay where you are!

The silhouette leaps. Rhee lunges. Osei drops the camera. Dolores raises the mop. They collide at the lip of the deep end in a tangle of arms, mop handle and raincoat.

A bright flash from Osei's camera bursts across the tile. The man scrambles up the stairs. Rhee and Dolores sprawl together. Osei pulls herself up.

OSEI
He's gone!

RHEE
(breathing hard)
Not far.

Dolores sits, hand on her chest, mop still clutched.

DOLORES
Detective. I think I know that coat.
